  "intro": "Revolving a region about an axis makes a solid whose volume an integral captures. Disk method: revolving $y=f(x)$ about the x-axis gives $V=\\pi\\int_a^b [f(x)]^2\\,dx$. Washer method (region between $f$ (outer) and $g$ (inner)): $V=\\pi\\int_a^b \\big([f(x)]^2-[g(x)]^2\\big)\\,dx$. Shell method about the y-axis: $V=2\\pi\\int_a^b x\\,f(x)\\,dx$. Choose the method that matches the axis and makes the integral simplest.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "Find the volume when $y=\\sqrt{x}$ on $[0,4]$ is revolved about the x-axis (disk method).",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Disk radius is $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$, so $[f(x)]^2=x$.",
          "$V=\\pi\\int_0^4 x\\,dx=\\pi\\left[\\frac{x^2}{2}\\right]_0^4$.",
          "Evaluate: $\\pi\\cdot\\frac{16}{2}=8\\pi$."
        ],
        "answer": "$V=8\\pi$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "Find the volume when the region between $y=x$ and $y=x^2$ is revolved about the x-axis (washer).",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Outer radius $x$, inner radius $x^2$, on $[0,1]$.",
          "$V=\\pi\\int_0^1 (x^2-x^4)\\,dx=\\pi\\left[\\frac{x^3}{3}-\\frac{x^5}{5}\\right]_0^1$.",
          "Evaluate: $\\pi\\left(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5}\\right)=\\frac{2\\pi}{15}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$V=\\dfrac{2\\pi}{15}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "Use shells: region under $y=x^2$ on $[0,2]$ revolved about the y-axis.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Shell radius $x$, height $x^2$.",
          "$V=2\\pi\\int_0^2 x\\cdot x^2\\,dx=2\\pi\\int_0^2 x^3\\,dx$.",
          "Evaluate: $2\\pi\\left[\\frac{x^4}{4}\\right]_0^2=2\\pi\\cdot 4=8\\pi$."
        ],
        "answer": "$V=8\\pi$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 4,
      "prompt": "Volume: $y=x$ on $[0,3]$ about the x-axis (disk).",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "$V=\\pi\\int_0^3 x^2\\,dx=\\pi\\cdot 9=9\\pi$."
        ],
        "answer": "$9\\pi$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 5,
      "prompt": "Volume: $y=x^2$ on $[0,1]$ about the x-axis (disk).",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "$V=\\pi\\int_0^1 x^4\\,dx=\\frac{\\pi}{5}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\dfrac{\\pi}{5}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 6,
      "prompt": "Volume: region under $y=x$ on $[0,2]$ about the y-axis (shell).",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "$V=2\\pi\\int_0^2 x\\cdot x\\,dx=2\\pi\\cdot\\frac{8}{3}=\\frac{16\\pi}{3}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\dfrac{16\\pi}{3}$"
      }
    }
  ]
